# FeltPen
#
# '0' and 'O' are one bitmap, and so are 'l' and '|'. The most common way for a font to be unreadable in principle.
#
# From https://mdfs.net/Apps/Font/ (FeltPen), a collection of BBC fonts
# dated 1989 to 1991, held there as VDU 23 character definitions.
#
# Characters 32 to 126 (94 glyphs).
#
# Characters sharing one bitmap, which nothing can tell
# apart from the pixels alone:
#     '0', 'O'
#     'l', '|'

